# The sha256 of the vendors' macOS arm64 archives of OpenBao and Zitadel, for the hosted macOS runner,
# which has no Docker (scripts/dev/native-services.sh, ginsys/bronzeward#892). The release is the tag of
# OPENBAO_IMAGE and ZITADEL_IMAGE in versions.env, so there is one place to bump; the archive is checked
# against its sha256 before it is unpacked, so a new tag there fails the Safari run on the checksum until
# the two lines below name the new archives. A file of its own: the Linux fixture reads versions.env as a
# closed manifest and refuses a key it does not use. OpenBao's is the vendor's checksums.txt line,
# Zitadel's the digest GitHub records for the release asset.
OPENBAO_DARWIN_ARM64_SHA256=7e648d6c93320ab66ced394fd88528c7122b7c1d991605c8e9b3845262459905
ZITADEL_DARWIN_ARM64_SHA256=e9de33e9278eed5d16cacc47c3ef5906d6e0bcaf2888b04a257ae0e6dc77f297
